============================================================================================
ANTIPODAL / CRT FOLD INTERPRETATION
============================================================================================
The quotient t~t+1/2 is not a new theorem by itself, but it forces an even/odd split.  Even speeds cover both sides of a pair in the same way.  Odd speeds must cover one side through a low band and the other through a high band.  At n=14 this pairs the 2-adic fold with the mod-7 unit cycle.

initial                  odd= 7 even= 6 14-gates= 0 pair_components=   7 pair_gap/th=0.000000
boundary 12->24          odd= 7 even= 6 14-gates= 0 pair_components=   7 pair_gap/th=0.000000
drop13 add14             odd= 6 even= 7 14-gates= 1 pair_components=  13 pair_gap/th=0.045455
drop13 add182            odd= 6 even= 7 14-gates= 1 pair_components=  25 pair_gap/th=0.065934
seven-ladder             odd= 8 even= 5 14-gates= 5 pair_components=  61 pair_gap/th=0.005411
seven with 42            odd= 8 even= 5 14-gates= 5 pair_components=  51 pair_gap/th=0.008163
S380 gate ladder         odd= 1 even=12 14-gates=12 pair_components=  71 pair_gap/th=0.002706

Creative target: prove that any n=14 row with enough even/14-gate mass to kill unit points leaves an antipodal high-band deficit unless it imports odd unit columns; those odd columns are exactly the local fan-tax columns in the 14-gate cover.

============================================================================================
NEW PROOF MODELS GENERATED
============================================================================================
1. Gate fan tax.
   Before a 14-gate can help globally, its own endpoints demand a local cover of size eight: six unit residues, 7, and an even bridge.
2. Product-depth debt.
   The S380 ladder pays every small-denominator row and uses only forced columns, but leaves debt at {2:+1,7:+1} and {2:+3,7:+1}.
3. Antipodal CRT fold.
   The even fold t~t+1/2 separates even columns from odd high/low columns.  For n=14 the missing proof should couple this with the mod-7 unit cycle.
4. Owner-charge descent.
   Endpoint debt should be charged to owner speeds, not just to the set as a whole.  Gate-heavy candidates expose which owners export which denominator depths.

